      {
        "h_title": "What is cendol",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Cendol is a Southeast Asian dessert popular for its green jelly noodles made from rice flour and pandan. It’s served chilled with coconut milk and shaved ice, making it a refreshing treat that doubles as a drink.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "The exact origin of cendol is unclear, as some debate its origins in Indonesia while others claim it originated in Malaysia.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "I don’t mind where it originated, I’m just happy Thailand has its own version! In Thailand, we call it lod chong, in Indonesia it’s called cendol, and in Vietnam it’s known as che banh lot.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Thai Lod chong",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Making Thai dessert recipes is always super fun, especially with kids around. This is one of those unique pandan desserts you can turn into an amusing afternoon family activity.",
            "url": "https://hungryinthailand.com/category/thai-desserts/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://hungryinthailand.com/category/thai-desserts/",
                "anchor_text": "Thai dessert recipes"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "I’ve made sure this recipe is easy to follow for everyone, even those who are new to Thai cuisine. As always, you can simply use the step-by-step images to guide you.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "The first step for making pandan noodles is extracting pandan juice, which is easy when using a blender. Next, we’ll mix rice flour and tapioca starch with the pandan juice to create a fragrant green dough.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "After preparing the dough, we’ll cook it until it reaches a somewhat slimy texture. Once cooked, this green mixture is transformed into noodles.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Traditionally, a lod chong press is used to shape the pandan dough into noodles. However, if you don’t have one, there’s no need to worry! I’ve found a simple method that you can use instead. You can find this alternative after the instructions section, so make sure to read on.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Once your noodle strands are ready, it’s as good as done. What’s left is to simply mix them with salted coconut milk, prepared sugar syrup, and crushed ice for a bowl full of creamy and sweet goodness!",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Cendol drink",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "The best thing about this dessert is how we can easily turn it into a refreshing drink.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Lod chong drink, or cendol drink, is extremely popular in Southeast Asia. It’s perfect for kids, and you can make it your own creation by topping it with jackfruit, beans, and even tapioca pearls – just like bubble tea!",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Simply add the pandan noodles to a chilled glass, pour in some of that delicious coconut milk and sweet sugar syrup, and top if off with crushed ice.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "That’s all! It’s great for family gatherings, especially on warm summer days, and you can even make it in advance.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Learn Thai cooking step by step",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "My cookbook is a combination of authentic Thai recipes and Western dishes cooked with Thai flavors and ingredients. It’s a great starting point if you’re new to Thai cooking or want to cook it more often.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Ingredients",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Ingredients can be sourced at Asian grocery stores and Asian markets.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "The exact measurements are in the recipe card at the end of this post.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Pandan noodles",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Step 1 : Make limewater by stirring calcium hydroxide into water until it dissolves. Let it sit for 3 hours.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 2 : Pour off 5 cups of the clear limewater, leaving the sediment. Blend 4 cups with chopped pandan leaves. Save 1 cup for later.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 3 : Strain the pandan leaf mix into a bowl using cheesecloth.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 4 : Mix tapioca starch and rice flour in a big bowl.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 5 : While kneading, slowly add some of the pandan water from step 3 to the flour mix to make a dough.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 6 : Add the rest of the pandan water to the dough.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 7 : Transfer the pandan water to a cooking pot and place it over the lowest heat possible, stirring continuously.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 8 : After about 10 minutes on the heat, the mixture will thicken and begin to clump together. Now, slowly add the cup of limewater you set aside earlier, a little every 3 minutes, and keep stirring without stopping. After 30 minutes of continuous stirring, you’ll see the mixture turn a bright green color and become gooey.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Step 9 : Put the dough through a lod chong press into ice-cold water.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Sugar syrup",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Step 10 : Now, we’ll make the sugar syrup. Place a saucepan over low-medium heat and add water and coconut sugar. Let this simmer for 3–5 minutes until it thickens slightly.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Salted coconut milk",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Step 11 : We will now make the coconut milk mixture. In a saucepan over low heat, add coconut milk, salt, and pandan leaves. Allow the coconut milk to cook for about 3 minutes.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Serve",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Step 12 : Drain the noodles. In a bowl, add ice, then noodles, coconut milk, and syrup to taste. Top with jackfruit, corn, or other toppings if you like. Enjoy!",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Kitchenware",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Blender for blending pandan leaves into a green colored juice",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Saucepan for making sugar syrup and salted coconut milk",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Pot with tool for stirring for cooking the noodle mixture",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
