      {
        "h_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Make this Thai lod chong dessert (cendol recipe) with pandan noodles and coconut milk. Learn how to turn it into a refreshing drink for hot days!",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "PANDAN NOODLES",
        "main_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Make limewater by stirring calcium hydroxide into water until it dissolves. Let it sit for 3 hours.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Pour off 5 cups of the clear limewater, leaving the sediment. Blend 4 cups with chopped pandan leaves. Save 1 cup for later.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Strain the pandan leaf mix into a bowl using cheesecloth.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Mix tapioca starch and rice flour in a big bowl.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "While kneading, slowly add some of the pandan water from step 3 to the flour mix to make a dough.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Add the rest of the pandan water to the dough.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Transfer the pandan water to a cooking pot and place it over the lowest heat possible, stirring continuously.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "After about 10 minutes on the heat, the mixture will thicken and begin to clump together. Now, slowly add the cup of limewater you set aside earlier, a little every 3 minutes, and keep stirring without stopping. After 30 minutes of continuous stirring, you’ll see the mixture turn a bright green color and become gooey.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Put the dough through a lod chong press into ice-cold water.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Thai Lod Chong Dessert (Cendol Recipe)",
